The `llm-council` bundled skill (SKILL.md and references/) is original Baton work
that learns from four upstream projects. Attribution and licensing for each:

1. llm-council — https://github.com/karpathy/llm-council
   Andrej Karpathy. The originating method: several independent answers,
   anonymous peer ranking, and a chairman synthesis. Credited as the source of
   the idea; no text or code is included.

2. llm-council-skill — https://github.com/gcpdev/llm-council-skill
   Copyright (c) 2026 Gustavo Publio — MIT License (reproduced in full below).
   references/external-seats.md adapts its approach to external-model seats:
   prefer a provider CLI, fall back to the provider HTTP API with
   OPENAI_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY and OPENAI_MODEL / GEMINI_MODEL overrides
   from the environment, and continue with the remaining seats when one
   provider fails. Those derived parts are offered under the MIT terms below
   and are NOT covered by Baton's AGPL-3.0-or-later terms.

3. llm-council-skill — https://github.com/tenfoldmarc/llm-council-skill
   Published without a license. Only methodology ideas were used (thinking-
   style lenses chosen to create tension, workspace context enrichment,
   parallel advisors, shuffled anonymized peer review, verdict sections with a
   single first step, a saved transcript and optional HTML report). All wording
   in this skill was written independently; no text was copied.

4. llm-council — https://github.com/Txnishkk93/llm-council
   Published without a license. Only methodology ideas were used (stances
   adapted to the question rather than a fixed set, a parseable "FINAL
   RANKING:" block with an average-rank tally, not manufacturing disagreement,
   and honesty that inline role-play is a single model). All wording in this
   skill was written independently; no text was copied.

Everything else in this skill — prior-verdict recall, grounded claims with
reviewer false-claim checks, the diversity re-seat, seat types, budget tiers,
confidence and "what would overturn it", persistence to .baton/council/ and
shared memory, and the never-act-without-the-user gate — is Baton's own work
under Baton's license.

Content-scanner note: Baton's skill scanner reports `credential-access` findings
for this skill (references/external-seats.md and the "No secrets" rule in
SKILL.md). They are expected: the text names API-key environment variables and
tells the agent to scrub secrets from the brief. The skill never reads, prints
or stores a credential value.

Keep the credits footer in SKILL.md when editing: it is the copy of this notice
that travels with an installed skill.

